      "text": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef main():\n    vectors = np.load(\"vectors.npy\", mmap_mode=\"r\")\n    N, D = vectors.shape\n\n    # Precompute squared norms (float64 for accuracy in later subtraction)\n    # Load in chunks to keep memory bounded, but 8000x1024 float32 is only ~32MB,\n    # so we can safely load fully into memory once.\n    vecs = np.asarray(vectors, dtype=np.float32)  # ensure real array in memory (~32MB)\n\n    norms = np.einsum('ij,ij->i', vecs, vecs, dtype=np.float64)\n\n    total_upper = 0.0\n    block_size = 400  # tuned for memory/time balance\n\n    for bi in range(0, N, block_size):\n        bj_end = N\n        block = vecs[bi:bi+block_size]          # shape (rows, D)\n        rest = vecs[bi:bj_end]                  # shape (cols, D), cols = N - bi\n        rows = block.shape[0]\n        cols = rest.shape[0]\n\n        # Compute dot products: rows x cols\n        dot = block @ rest.T  # float32 matmul, shape (rows, cols)\n\n        # squared distances using norms\n        n_block = norms[bi:bi+rows]             # shape (rows,)\n        n_rest = norms[bi:bj_end]               # shape (cols,)\n\n        sq_dist = n_block[:, None] + n_rest[None, :] - 2.0 * dot.astype(np.float64)\n        np.maximum(sq_dist, 0.0, out=sq_dist)\n        dist = np.sqrt(sq_dist)\n\n        # We only want j_local > i_local (strict upper triangle within this block-vs-rest matrix)\n        # local indices: i_local corresponds to global bi+i_local\n        #                j_local corresponds to global bi+j_local\n        # condition: (bi+j_local) > (bi+i_local)  =>  j_local > i_local\n        # Use triu with k=1 mask\n        mask = np.triu(np.ones((rows, cols), dtype=bool), k=1)\n        total_upper += dist[mask].sum(dtype=np.float64)\n\n    total = 2.0 * total_upper\n\n    # Print as decimal value (float), formatted plainly\n    print(f\"TOTAL:{total:.10f}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
